<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέθω</span></b> , impf.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤρεθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					3.84
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), 
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέθεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.618
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				1103
			</span></i> :—poet. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεθίζω,</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>
			<i>stir to anger, provoke,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μ᾽ ἔρεθε, σχετλίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.414
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτ᾽ ἄν μ᾽ ἐρέθῃσιν ὀνειδείοις
					ἐπέεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.519
				</span></i>
			 ; in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> of all sources of <i>disquiet,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδυνάων.., αἵ μ᾽ ἐρέθουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.813
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελεδῶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.517
				</span></i>
			 : c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				8.14
			</span></i> : c. acc. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤρεθον
			ᾠδάν</span> they <i>raised</i> a song, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				21.21
			</span></i> codd. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐρωμανίην</span>
			<i>increase</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.255
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>explore, search,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰλυούς</span>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέοντες</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				143
			</span></i>.</div>
